"Original work": The work or software distributed or communicated by the licensor under this Licence, available as source code and also as executable code as the case may be.

"Derivative works": Any work or software that could be created by the licensee, based upon the Original work or modifications thereof. This Licence does not define how extensive the modifications must be in order for a work to be classified as a Derivative work; this extent is determined by copyright law applicable in the country mentioned in Article 15.

"The work": The Original work or any Derivative works.

"The licensor": The natural or legal person, public authority, agency, or any other entity that distributes or communicates the work under the Licence.

"Licensee" or "You": Any natural or legal person who possesses a copy of the work and exercises any rights granted under this Licence.

"Distribution" or "Communication": The provision to third parties of a copy of the work, in any form or by any means, such as download, broadcast, streaming, or any other form of on-line or off-line distribution, or inclusion in other software or applications, or making available to be used as a service or software-as-a-service (SaaS).

Article 1 – Subject-matter of the Licence

The Licence applies to any Original work distributed or communicated by the licensor under the terms of this Licence.

