Article 5 – Obligations of the licensee

The exercise of the rights granted to the licensee is subject to some restrictions and obligations. Those obligations are the following:

The licensee shall retain in full all copyright, patent or trademarks notices, and all notices that refer to the Licence and to the disclaimer of warranties. The licensee must include a copy of such notices and of the Licence with every copy of the work he/she distributes or communicates. The licensee must cause any Derivative works to carry prominent notices stating that the work has been modified and the date of modification.

The licensee must cause the Derivative works to be licensed under the terms of this Licence or of a later version of this Licence unless the Derivative work is distributed under a compatible licence. A "compatible licence" is a licence that satisfies the requirements of Article 5 of the EUPL, providing that the licence also guarantees, in principle, that the work can be relicensed under that compatible licence.

The licensee who distributes or communicates Derivative works in source code form under the provisions of Article 5.2 must make that source code easily accessible, in a repository. The source code must remain accessible for at least as long as the licensor continues to distribute or communicate the Original work.

Article 6 – Attribution rights

The licensor shall respect your moral rights.

Article 7 – Disclaimer of Warranty

